---
import MainLayout from "../layout/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Jakub Olszewski's about">
  <div class="w-6/12 mx-auto">
    <section>
      <h1 class="text-5xl">About</h1>
      <img
        src="/images/studyfront-project-image.png"
        width="500"
        class="my-2 shadow-md drop-shadow-[10px_10px_35px_rgba(1,1,1,0.2)]"
        alt=""
      />
      <header>
        <p>About</p>
        <h1>Hey, I'm [Your Name].</h1>
        <p>
          A web development student about to graduate. I've spent the last few
          years learning how to build things for the web, and I'm now looking
          for the chance to do that for real.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>What I Build</h2>
        <p>
          Most of what I've worked on lives in the JavaScript world —
          component-driven frontends and the APIs behind them. I'm comfortable
          across the stack and still actively figuring out where I want to go
          deep.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, React, Node.js, Express, and
          MongoDB.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Selected Projects</h2>

        <article>
          <h3>Project One</h3>
          <p>
            A full-stack app built around API integration and user
            authentication, with a responsive UI that works across devices.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Project Two</h3>
          <p>
            A frontend project centered on reusable components and smooth,
            intuitive interactions.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Project Three</h3>
          <p>
            A backend-focused build where I worked through API design, database
            structure, and server-side logic.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How I Work</h2>
        <p>
          I try to write code that's simple and easy to follow — not just for
          me, but for whoever reads it next. I care about accessibility, browser
          consistency, and not overcomplicating things.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm finishing my degree and these projects represent where I am right
          now. I don't have years of production experience yet, but I'm serious
          about the craft and keen to keep improving.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Let's Connect</h2>
        <p>Always happy to chat or hear about opportunities.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#">GitHub</a></li>
          <li><a href="#">LinkedIn</a></li>
          <li><a href="mailto:">Email</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </section>
  </div>
</MainLayout>
